diff --git a/docs/ModernizationBatch.md b/docs/ModernizationBatch.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7e0c788
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ModernizationBatch.md
@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+# Verified modernization batch
+
+Baseline: `5be8f749c42d762caf4d1b500e0c4cc357c169d8` (includes PRs #1/#2).
+The development snapshot contains 793 tracked blobs, each checked against its
+Git object hash before editing. This is now a full source checkout, not the
+partial fixture used for the earlier C23/SIMD proposal.
+
+## Implemented
+
+C23 and C++26 are required for project-owned targets. The maintained Teakra
+copy also uses C++26. Existing C vendored code is compiled, not rewritten in
+another language. No reflection, std::simd or new handwritten assembler is
+required. Module scanning is disabled because this project has no module units.
+
+- Fix C++26 incomplete-type unique_ptr initialization at GPU/DSi SD boundaries
+  by moving completeness-requiring initialization to source definitions.
+- Replace a cross-enum bitwise operation in firmware defaults with
+  `std::to_underlying`, preserving the original bits.
+- Preserve the earlier capture/JIT/savestate/bitfield/UTF-8 fixes, and correct
+  software capture dirty indexing to use the same wrapped VRAM address as data.
+- Provide alias-safe paired-pixel conversion plus optional AVX2 and AVX-512F
+  intrinsics; compile capabilities and runtime CPU/OS state are both checked.
+  SIMD variants do not impose a global ISA requirement on the binary.
+- Serialize shared network-driver operations and replacement/destruction;
+  keep the DriverMutex -> Dispatcher lock order. Validate queue indices and
+  lengths, and read the registration mask under the same lock as its queues.
+  Callers must still stop operations before destroying the Net object.
+- Avoid Teakra's atomic exchange when no interrupt is pending, without weakening
+  sequential consistency. Share immutable opcode decoder metadata across
+  instances; every handler still receives its own interpreter. No DSP timing,
+  instruction handler, repeat rule, callback schedule or state format is changed.
+
+## Host options and toolchains
+
+`ENABLE_ASM` defaults ON; disabling it disables the native ARM JIT, whose linkage
+requires assembler. It does not prohibit compiler-generated machine code or
+assembler in separately built dependencies. `ENABLE_SIMD`/`ENABLE_AVX2` default
+ON, `ENABLE_AVX512` defaults OFF. Non-x86/unsupported compilers use scalar code.
+An explicit unavailable SIMD selector returns the scalar implementation.
+
+`release-clang` chooses Clang for C, C++ and assembler. The optional
+`MELONDS_CURRENT_TOOLCHAIN` profile checks the 2026-09-07 release floors:
+Clang 23.1.0 or GCC 16.2, and CMake 4.4.3. It does not install software. The
+current-build CI helper uses exact LLVM archive hashes and exact version checks;
+GCC 14 remains a compatibility/reference build, not a claim to be GCC 16.
+No global -march=native, AVX requirement or fast-math flag is introduced.
+
+## Executed local verification
+
+All results below are from the complete checkout. Local tools: GCC 14.2,
+Clang 17, CMake 3.31.6, x86-64 EPYC 9V74 VM.
+
+| Configuration | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Complete core + maintained Teakra, Clang Release, JIT and AVX-512 allowed | 21/21 CTest entries |
+| Complete core + Teakra, GCC Release, ASM/JIT and SIMD disabled | 19/19 |
+| Standalone boundary tests, Clang ASan/UBSan, SIMD allowed | 17/17 |
+| Bundled libslirp 4.8.0/custom glib, standalone C23 build | Compiled successfully |
+
+Actual headless core tests execute hand-authored ARM code, count to 100 and
+store the result. Interpreter, JIT and fast-memory JIT each run real scheduled
+frames, save, corrupt RAM, restore, and run again. The software display path
+checks every pixel of a 49,152-pixel constant VRAM framebuffer. The expected
+RGB555 31 -> RGB666 62 -> output 251 behavior is retained, not rounded to 255.
+These tests use FreeBIOS and explicit test-only platform stubs; no commercial
+ROM, firmware dump, real network, filesystem mutation or GPU context is used.
+
+Real Teakra interpreter before/after traces match for NOPs, repeated execution,
+an expansion word, a timed normal IRQ, vectored IRQ and save/restore. State
+bytes, program reads, stack writes and component ticks are compared. This is
+not exhaustive DSP instruction coverage or a physical DS/DSi oracle.
+
+Queue tests fail on the original source (unregistered receiver crash and
+concurrent fake-driver calls) and pass after the changes. Sanitizers here cover
+the focused boundary suite, NOT every complete-core instruction path. Thread
+Sanitizer and real multiplayer sessions were not run locally.
+
+## Measured performance
+
+GCC 14.2, same `-std=c++2c -O3 -fwrapv -DNDEBUG -pthread` flags, one pinned
+logical CPU, warmup and nine shuffled paired runs. All 18 Teakra NOP checksums
+agree. Median instruction time: 10.4652 ns -> 8.0077 ns (23.48% reduction).
+This is an interpreter-loop microbenchmark, NOT DSi game FPS or a JIT result.
+
+Earlier same-flags pixel-kernel tests measured AVX2 around 54-56% and AVX-512
+around 59-69% shorter routine time than the original paired-pixel routine;
+the alias-safe scalar fallback was about 1-3% slower. Those earlier measurements
+are not new end-to-end results. Prefer application profiling before expanding
+this optimization to unrelated kernels. No DSP JIT is included.
+
+## Dependencies and portability
+
+vcpkg is pinned to `04a9d8e5212d01ee1dd9478eadd9caade4f8b0d4`.
+Remove the obsolete FAAD2 2.11.1 overlay: upstream 2.11.2 now installs its
+pkg-config file on Windows. The explicit maintenance helper reproduces the
+libarchive 3.8.9 overlay from a Git-blob-verified registry port and a
+SHA256-verified official release archive, then validates the inherited patches.
+An overlay is a build recipe, not evidence that an application build succeeded.
+
+The `release-current-deps` profile uses externally installed Qt >=6.11.2;
+this avoids claiming that the registry's Qt 6.11.1 is latest. Generic builds
+can still use the pinned registry Qt. Resolved versions from actual builds
+are recorded by `tools/ci-current-build.py`. Do not conflate apt packages,
+registry versions, external Qt and vendored modified libraries.
+
+Qt 6.11 requires macOS 13: recommended triplets and the default deployment
+target are updated accordingly. Older explicit triplets remain available but
+are not a compatibility promise for new Qt. SDL2 -> SDL3, bundled custom slirp,
+FatFs, GL loaders and Teakra are not blindly overwritten by upstream copies.
+
+## Remote publication status (2026-09-07)
+
+The full-source export workflow succeeded. A later connector `create_commit`
+request for the consolidated modernization batch was blocked because the tool
+could not determine its security status. No ref update or new PR followed.
+The remote maintenance branch remains at
+`1656729ca2e8edd8a4fc13bfe2b8a5450ec20df0`, containing only the development
+source-export workflow on top of PR #2. The emulator changes in this delivery
+are local changes, NOT a published commit. Neither the current-build helper
+nor the libarchive overlay generator ran. In particular the generated
+libarchive 3.8.9 overlay is not present or verified in this source tree.
+The archive excludes the temporary development-export workflow. Existing
+upstream build workflows have not been replaced or globally disabled.
+
+## Remaining verification boundaries
+
+Check CI on the exact published commit separately. No claim of complete
+Windows/macOS/BSD success is implied by Linux core tests. Real DS/DSi,
+commercial-game playback, complete malformed-state handling, DSP JIT,
+OpenGL/compute output and GPU-readback performance remain separate acceptance
+requirements. Retain baseline behavior unless hardware evidence justifies a
+change. All-code optimality and zero possible regression are not proven.
